    {
      "id": "s1-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "BEN — Just Like a Dream",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서는 **-처럼**을 배워요.\n비교할 때 쓰는 표현이에요. '~같이', '~처럼'이라는 뜻이에요.\n\nBEN의 **Just Like a Dream**은\n꿈처럼 사라질까 봐 두려운 사랑 이야기예요.",
      "contentEnglish": "In this lesson, you'll learn **-처럼** — used for comparisons meaning 'like' or 'as.'\n\nBEN's Just Like a Dream is about a love that feels so fragile, it might disappear like a dream.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-line1",
      "type": "line-breakdown",
      "label": "가사 읽기",
      "lyricLine": "눈을 뜨면 희미해져 버릴 꿈처럼 놔줘",
      "breakdown": "눈을 뜨면 = when I open my eyes\n희미해져 버릴 = will become faint / fade away\n꿈처럼 = like a dream (**-처럼**!)\n놔줘 = let go / leave it\n\n\"Let it go like a dream that will fade when I open my eyes.\"\n\n**-처럼** attaches to nouns to mean 'like' or 'as.'",
      "dictionary": [
        {
          "word": "눈을 뜨다",
          "reading": "눈을 뜨다",
          "meaning": "to open one's eyes"
        },
        {
          "word": "희미하다",
          "reading": "희미하다",
          "meaning": "to be faint / dim"
        },
        {
          "word": "꿈",
          "reading": "꿈",
          "meaning": "dream"
        },
        {
          "word": "-처럼",
          "reading": "-처럼",
          "meaning": "like, as"
        }
      ]
    },
